  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business and Peace in Colombia- Ideas for Peace Foundation (FIP) - 2017-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Business and Peace in Colombia- Ideas for Peace Foundation (FIP) - 2017-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta projektst&#xf6;d till Ide&#xe9;r f&#xf6;r Fredsstiftelsen (FIP) syftar till att fr&#xe4;mja en aktiv roll f&#xf6;r ekonomiska akt&#xf6;rer i uppbyggnaden av en h&#xe5;llbar fred i Colombia genom fyra resultat. F&#xf6;r det f&#xf6;rsta, &quot;l&#xe4;ra k&#xe4;nna&quot; genom att identifiera en baslinje av initiativ och intressen inom f&#xf6;retagssektorn p&#xe5; nationell niv&#xe5; och i prioriterade regioner. F&#xf6;r det andra, genom att ta fram tekniska bidrag och praktiska verktyg f&#xf6;r att uppmuntra f&#xf6;retagssektorns roll i fredsbyggandet (&quot;erk&#xe4;nna och anpassa&quot;). F&#xf6;r det tredje, genom att utveckla den regionala agendan f&#xf6;r fredsbyggande (&quot;fr&#xe5;n ord till handling&quot;). Slutligen, genom att l&#xe5;ta den privata sektorn delta i genomf&#xf6;randet av den offentliga fredsagendan genom att dokumentera och replikera erfarenheter (&quot;l&#xe4;ra och replikera&quot;). Detta &#xe4;r den andra fasen av Sidas bidrag med ID-nummer: 55190017.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project support to Ideas for Peace Foundation (FIP) aims at promoting an active role of economic actors in the building of a sustainable peace in Colombia through four outputs or successive steps. First, &#x201c;get to know&#x201d; by identifying a baseline of initiatives and interests of the business sector at a national level and with prioritized regions. Secondly, by producing technical inputs and practical tools to encourage the role of the business sector in peace building (&quot;acknowledge and adapt&quot;). Thirdly, by developing the regional peace building agenda (&#x201c;from words to action&#x201d;). Finally, by including the private sector in the implementation of the public peace agenda, through documenting and replicating experiences (&#x201c;learn and replicate&#x201d;).

This is the second phase of Sida&#x2019;s contribution 55190017.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to promote the active role of businesses in helping to build a sustainable peace process in Colombia through four outputs or successive steps. First, get to know by identifying a baseline of initiatives and interests of the business sector at a national level and with prioritized regions (Development Programs with a Territorial Approach  PDET regions). Secondly, by producing technical inputs and practical tools to encourage the role of the business sector in peace building (acknowledge and adapt). Thirdly, by developing the regional peace building agenda (from words to action). Finally, by including the private sector in the implementation of the public peace agenda, by documenting and replicating experiences (learn and replicate).</narrative>
  </description>
